ls-since-2021", "url": "https://t.co/7iMyp6Gnw5"}]}, "id": "2120215272191865225", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1079, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Demographics uber alles\nhttps://t.co/7iMyp6Gnw5", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2120215272191865225"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:00:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120214933304754687"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 48, "id": "18378349", "start": 32, "username": "KeithMcCullough"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/keithmcculloug…", "end": 72, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/keithmccullough/status/2120214753209712668", "start": 49, "url": "https://t.co/sy9YXCVHt9"}]}, "id": "2120214933304754687", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 11328, "like_count": 17, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120214753209712668", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Great convo, as always … thanks @KeithMcCullough https://t.co/sy9YXCVHt9", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2120214933304754687"}, {"author_id": "2220183580", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:57:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120214210277749197"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/ft/status/2120…", "end": 242, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/ft/status/2120191719916327246", "start": 219, "url": "https://t.co/ZjrKmJCR9d"}]}, "id": "2120214210277749197", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 3151, "like_count": 29, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 6}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120191719916327246", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "It’s a nonsense is what it is. There’s nothing here that isn’t the subject of conventional economic analysis and thinking in which ppl have different views. We don’t need clickbait labels like ‘anti fascist economics’. https://t.co/ZjrKmJCR9d", "url": "https://x.com/georgemagnus1/status/2120214210277749197"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:51:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120212883997123061"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/rTkd9BMRGd", "end": 284, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120212883997123061/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120212709988007936", "start": 261, "url": "https://t.co/rTkd9BMRGd"}]}, "id": "2120212883997123061", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1846, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Young people labor market update:\n\n1/ It's been tough for people in their early 20s with a 4 year degree, but their corner of the labor market is finally improving.\n\nOver the past 11 months their unemployment rate averaged 6.58%, down from 6.76% a year earlier https://t.co/rTkd9BMRGd", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120212883997123061"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:44:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120210895972499874"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/8e064TXq62", "end": 218, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120210895972499874/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120210890897408000", "start": 195, "url": "https://t.co/8e064TXq62"}]}, "id": "2120210895972499874", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1180, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Private sector employment growth measured by ADP slowed from mid-September to late October, but remains stronger than it was over the summer... consistent with further unemployment rate declines https://t.co/8e064TXq62", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120210895972499874"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:00:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120199867914199097"], "id": "2120199867914199097", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 42, "impression_count": 64154, "like_count": 509, "quote_count": 13, "reply_count": 97, "retweet_count": 15}, "text": "Would it be fair to characterize the state of enterprise AI adoption as: \n\n\"We don't really know if we're getting any return from all this spending, but our employees would lose their shit if we took the tools away?\"", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120199867914199097"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:56:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120198873360585059"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/TheStalwart/st…", "end": 84, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/TheStalwart/status/2120197613307711913", "start": 61, "url": "https://t.co/aVxARmHsqv"}]}, "id": "2120198873360585059", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 11334, "like_count": 75, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 10}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120197613307711913", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "*TREASURY 2-YEAR YIELD RISES 20 BASIS POINTS ON DAY TO 4.77% https://t.co/aVxARmHsqv", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120198873360585059"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:55:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120198795233255703"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 76, "start": 73, "tag": "AI"}], "urls": [{"description": "Regulators target black-hat generative engine optimization as marketers manipulate algorithms to invent products and inflate rankings", "display_url": "caixinglobal.com/2026-11-06/in-…", "end": 218, "expanded_url": "https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-11-06/in-depth-china-cracks-down-on-poisoning-ai-chatbots-with-fake-marketing-102501857.html", "images": [{"height": 373, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120198801881206785/I7HfVwIZ?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 560}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120198801881206785/I7HfVwIZ?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 195, "status": 200, "title": "In Depth: China Cracks Down on ‘Poisoning’ AI Chatbots With Fake Marketing", "unwound_url": "https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-11-06/in-depth-china-cracks-down-on-poisoning-ai-chatbots-with-fake-marketing-102501857.html", "url": "https://t.co/aeqNhN2MbK"}]}, "id": "2120198795233255703", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1146, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "\"Chinese authorities are penalizing companies that deliberately “poison” #AI search results, cracking down on a new frontier of corporate fraud known as black-hat generative engine optimization\"\nhttps://t.co/aeqNhN2MbK", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2120198795233255703"}, {"author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:54:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120198542920970508"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 250, "id": "174586205", "start": 234, "username": "OxfordEconomics"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/RUasYgfqp8", "end": 274, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120198542920970508/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120198446409830400", "start": 251, "url": "https://t.co/RUasYgfqp8"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/RUasYgfqp8", "end": 274, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120198542920970508/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120198465187680256", "start": 251, "url": "https://t.co/RUasYgfqp8"}]}, "id": "2120198542920970508", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 3896, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Oxford Economics expects a record El Niño to leave lasting scars, with world GDP falling to a trough near 0.9% below baseline in 2028 and staying about 0.7% lower through 2031, as emerging economies bear the persistent loss.\n\nSource: @OxfordEconomics https://t.co/RUasYgfqp8", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120198542920970508"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:51:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120197613307711913"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/MmkkHx1pCt", "end": 89, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120197613307711913/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120197568701362176", "start": 66, "url": "https://t.co/MmkkHx1pCt"}]}, "id": "2120197613307711913", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 13, "impression_count": 97138, "like_count": 147, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 21}, "text": "We're seeing the biggest one-day jump in 2-year yields since 2024 https://t.co/MmkkHx1pCt", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120197613307711913"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:30:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120192425792868414"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/MkOcwA5sHK", "end": 223, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120192425792868414/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120192167821885440", "start": 200, "url": "https://t.co/MkOcwA5sHK"}, {"display_url": "x.com/AntoineBondaz/…", "end": 247, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/AntoineBondaz/status/2120109004143616068", "start": 224, "url": "https://t.co/IsxzPMj4v2"}]}, "id": "2120192425792868414", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 4283, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120109004143616068", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I prefer to look at the trailing 12m sum --and on that measure, China's surplus with the EU in the 12ms to October was $360b, up $75b y/y\n\n(and up $200b or a pp or so of EU GDP v pre pandemic levels) https://t.co/MkOcwA5sHK https://t.co/IsxzPMj4v2", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120192425792868414"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:27:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120191753420509375"], "id": "2120191753420509375", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18314, "like_count": 142, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 23, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Wonder how much better the election would’ve been for republicans if food prices weren’t ripping in the weeks leading up to the vote", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120191753420509375"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:20:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120189753132036155"], "id": "2120189753132036155", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2623, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "MOFCOM West accounts are entertaining", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120189753132036155"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:11:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120187714532442430"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/3XVc5vNIdc", "end": 228, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120187714532442430/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120187693409636352", "start": 205, "url": "https://t.co/3XVc5vNIdc"}, {"display_url": "x.com/GagnonMacro/st…", "end": 252, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/GagnonMacro/status/2120170965967495252", "start": 229, "url": "https://t.co/hve2ApMkPc"}]}, "id": "2120187714532442430", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 4290, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120170965967495252", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "net of gold imports, China's surplus in manufactures is  more less back where it was relative to China's own economy during the initial China shock years (it is obviously way bigger relative to world GDP) https://t.co/3XVc5vNIdc https://t.co/hve2ApMkPc", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120187714532442430"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:05:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120186072365662481"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/sophiacai99/st…", "end": 294, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/sophiacai99/status/2120154675098071431", "start": 271, "url": "https://t.